# Identity (FHP-Specification#6): this file describes the FHP *development*
# repository only. It carries no DOI of its own — this repository publishes no
# GitHub releases or tags and no FHP Zenodo/Zenodo-concept record exists, and
# none is implied here. The registered bibliographic titles in `references`
# below ("FHR Specification", "FAIR-bioHeaders Specification") belong to the
# shared publication lineage; FHP work must not rename them, and they do not
# identify this development repository. Cite the published FHP contract through
# the FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification release that carries it.
#
# Source provenance (#6 / #2 / FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#107 handoff): the
# FHP contract bytes in this tree are pinned compatibility copies of the shared
# v0.5.0 release commit 170e677fbb6726a3f765373dbe1f214820000be7 (annotated tag
# object 7150f74cf447de5694b8938c705d5a5896eaeacd, released 2026-11-04), per
# docs/DEVELOPMENT-TREE-PROPOSAL.md §3; machine-readable digests arrive with
# FHP-Specification#3 (provenance.json + shared-parity CI). Any future
# FHP-specific release record is a maintainer action coordinated through
# FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#107 (see also FHP-Specification#1).
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FHP Specification (development repository)
message: >-
  This repository develops the FHP (protein-set) header of the FAIR BioHeaders
  family; it has no release DOI of its own. Cite the released FHP contract as
  the FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification release carrying it (shared v0.4.0 for FHP
  schemaVersion 1.0, shared v0.5.0 for FHP 1.1) via its fixed
  https://w3id.org/fair-bioheaders/fhp/vX.Y.Z alias. The Zenodo records listed
  under `references` are FHR-lineage specification records kept as labeled
  related citations, not FHP identifiers. For the motivating publication cite
  the FHR paper in `references`. Historical USDA public-domain material
  remains public domain; applicable subsequent project contributions from
  March 2025 onward use MPL-2.0. Third-party terms and provenance details are
  documented in LICENSE.
type: dataset
authors:
- given-names: David
  family-names: Molik
  email: molik@fhref.org
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3192-6538
- given-names: Adam
  family-names: Wright
  email: wright@fhref.org
  affiliation: OICR
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5719-4024
# No `identifiers`, `doi`, `version` or `date-released`: this development
# repository publishes no release artifacts or DOI (tracked in
# FHP-Specification#6; do not borrow the FHR-lineage records below).
repository-code: https://github.com/FAIR-bioHeaders/FHP-Specification
url: https://github.com/FAIR-bioHeaders/FHP-Specification
abstract: >-
  The FAIR bioHeaders Protein set (FHP) standard embeds a small YAML metadata
  header inside protein FASTA files, validated against a per-type JSON Schema
  contract and covered by a checksum of the file's exact bytes. FHP
  distinguishes predicted, database and mixed protein sets and records source
  provenance without inferring quality-control results. This repository is the
  FHP development surface: the LinkML model, the FHP JSON-LD context and
  vocabulary, the HTML-microdata binding and the FHP conformance vectors are
  developed and served here, while the published FHP contract is released by
  FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification (schemaVersion 1.0 from shared release v0.4.0;
  schemaVersion 1.1 with x- extension fields from shared release v0.5.0).
keywords:
- FAIR
- TRUST
- protein
- proteome
- fasta
- yaml
- json
- json-ld
- microdata
license: MPL-2.0
# Historical permissions and third-party exceptions are documented in LICENSE.
